1
00:03:33,599 --> 00:03:39,599
Some fears haunt you from within.

2
00:07:07,199 --> 00:07:13,199
The Unfamiliar is a thriller, horror film directed by Henk Pretorius.

3
00:10:40,799 --> 00:10:46,799
A British Army doctor comes back from a war, thinking that she has PTSD only to discover that there
is a more daunting malevolence at work making the life that she knew unfamiliar.

4
00:14:14,399 --> 00:14:20,399
Elizabeth 'Izzy' Cormack, played by Jemima West.

5
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Ethan Cormack, played by Christopher Dane.

6
00:21:21,599 --> 00:21:27,599
Emma Cormack, played by Rebecca Hanssen.

7
00:24:55,200 --> 00:25:01,200
Tommy Cormack, played by Harry McMillan-Hunt.

8
00:28:28,799 --> 00:28:34,799
Auntie Mae, played by Rachel Lin.

9
00:32:02,399 --> 00:32:08,399
Kaimoni, played by Tori Butler-Hart.

10
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Dune (titled on-screen as Dune: Part One) is a 2021 American epic space opera film directed and
co-produced by Denis Villeneuve, who co-wrote the screenplay with Jon Spaihts and Eric Roth.

11
00:39:09,599 --> 00:39:15,599
It is the first of a two-part adaptation of the 1965 novel by Frank Herbert,
and the first installment of Villeneuve's Dune film trilogy.

12
00:42:43,199 --> 00:42:49,199
The cast includes Timothée Chalamet, Rebecca Ferguson, Oscar Isaac, Josh Brolin, Stellan Skarsgård, Dave Bautista, Stephen
McKinley Henderson, Zendaya, Chang Chen, Sharon Duncan-Brewster, Charlotte Rampling, Jason Momoa, and Javier Bardem.

13
00:46:16,799 --> 00:46:22,799
Set in the distant future, the film follows Paul Atreides as his family, the noble House
Atreides, is thrust into a war for the deadly and inhospitable desert planet Arrakis.

14
00:49:50,400 --> 00:49:56,400
The film is the third adaptation of Dune, following David Lynch's 1984
film and John Harrison's 2000 television miniseries.

15
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
After an unsuccessful attempt by Paramount Pictures to produce a new adaptation, Legendary Pictures acquired the
Dune film and television rights in 2016, with Villeneuve signing on as director in February 2017.

16
00:56:57,599 --> 00:57:03,599
Production contracts were secured only for the first film, relying
on its success before a sequel would be produced.

17
01:00:31,199 --> 01:00:37,199
Principal photography took place from March to July 2019 at locations
including Budapest, Jordan, Norway, and Abu Dhabi.

18
01:04:04,799 --> 01:04:10,799
Dune was scheduled for a late 2020 release, but was
delayed due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

19
01:07:38,400 --> 01:07:44,400
The film premiered at the 78th Venice International Film Festival on September 3, 2021, before its international release on
September 15, 2021; it was then released in United States theaters and streaming on HBO Max on October 22, 2021.

20
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
Dune grossed $411 million on a $165 million budget becoming
the tenth-highest-grossing film of 2021.

21
01:14:45,599 --> 01:14:51,599
It was positively received by critics and audiences.

22
01:18:19,199 --> 01:18:25,199
The film won six awards at the 94th Academy Awards and was nominated in
four other categories; it received numerous other accolades.

23
01:21:52,800 --> 01:21:58,800
A sequel, Dune: Part Two, was released on March 1, 2024, with another sequel, Dune:
Part Three, based on Herbert's 1969 novel Dune Messiah, in production.

24
01:25:26,399 --> 01:25:32,399
The tone is dark and intense.
